# ThreadSanitizer suppressions (TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=..., set by the tsan test preset). Every entry needs a
# justification. Prefer fixing the code; TSan runs nightly and is advisory (docs/testing.md).
#
# libarrow (conda-forge) is not built with TSan: the synchronization inside Arrow's thread pools and futures
# (e.g. the I/O pool that pre-buffers Parquet column chunks) is invisible to TSan, so a buffer that an Arrow I/O
# thread frees after the reader is done is reported as racing with the reader's earlier memcpy (first seen in the
# nightly of 2026-09-26: BaseMemoryPoolImpl<SystemAllocator>::Free vs snappy decompression). Ignore the
# interceptors (malloc/free/memcpy) called from libarrow itself; races in our code between our own threads are
# still reported.
called_from_lib:libarrow.so
